{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch6\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\",\n      \"purpose\": \"系统评估肠道微生物组特征与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）诱导的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）之间的关联，分析疗效与毒性的耦合或解耦关系，并探讨微生物干预策略（如 FMT、益生菌）在毒性管理中的安全性与情境依赖性。\",\n      \"scope\": \"聚焦于实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、胃肠道肿瘤等）患者接受 ICI 治疗期间，基线或动态微生物组与 irAEs（特别是结肠炎、心肌炎、皮肤毒性等）的观察性关联及干预试验中的安全性信号。涵盖微生物标志物预测价值、疗效 - 毒性权衡机制、供体特征对毒性的调节作用。排除血液系统恶性肿瘤为主的纯临床数据（除非用于机制类比），排除无微生物组数据的纯毒性流行病学研究。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0025\",\n        \"P0099\",\n        \"P0299\",\n        \"P0318\",\n        \"P0373\",\n        \"P0405\",\n        \"P0465\",\n        \"P0539\"\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"微生物组特征对 irAEs 的预测价值与癌种特异性\",\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"综述特定菌属与 irAEs 风险的关联证据：如 Ruminococcaceae 减少与严重 irAEs 相关（P0049），产丁酸菌缺失与结肠炎相关（P0017），以及 Bacteroides 在某些队列中与 irAEs 正相关但在其他队列中与疗效正相关的矛盾结果（P0239, P0313）。\",\n            \"强调癌种特异性：胃肠道癌症中 Ruminococcus callidus 富集与较低重症 irAEs 风险相关（P0011），而黑色素瘤中特定菌群（如 P. copri）与心肌炎风险相关（P0197, P0583）。\",\n            \"指出预测模型的开发与局限：如基于 14 种微生物特征的 irAEs 预测模型（RF14）（P0308），但需注明多重检验校正后显著性不足及队列异质性挑战（P0312, P0049）。\",\n            \"区分 irAEs 类型：结肠炎证据最强（P0072, P0278），心肌炎（P0051, P0149）、皮肤毒性（P0259）及神经毒性（P0530）的微生物证据有限或仅为相关性。\"\n          ],\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0011\",\n            \"P0017\",\n            \"P0049\",\n            \"P0072\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0239\",\n            \"P0278\",\n            \"P0308\",\n            \"P0312\",\n            \"P0530\",\n            \"P0583\"\n          ],\n          \"limitations\": \"多数证据为观察性关联，缺乏因果验证；不同研究间测序技术及 irAEs 定义标准（如 CTCAE 版本）存在异质性；特定菌属（如 Bacteroides）的作用方向在不同队列中不一致。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"疗效与毒性的耦合与解耦关系\",\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"分析'双刃剑'效应：某些微生物特征（如 Akkermansia 高丰度）既关联于延长 OS 又增加 irAEs 风险（P0260），提示免疫激活的共同生物学基础。\",\n            \"探讨解耦可能性：特定菌种（如 Eubacterium siraeum）可能与无 irAEs 的响应相关（P0239），SCFA 产生菌（F. prausnitzii）高丰度与无 irAEs 相关（P0428），挑战'毒性预示疗效'的直觉。\",\n            \"引入宿主免疫状态作为中介：irAEs 的多器官受累特征比单一毒性更能预测生存获益（P0465），微生物组可能通过调节全身免疫基调（如 Treg/Th17 平衡）同时影响疗效与毒性（P0120, P0333）。\",\n            \"结合纵向数据：拟杆菌属既与 Treg 减少（疗效）相关，又与严重 irAEs 相关（P0098），提示基线免疫稳态是关键调节因子。\"\n          ],\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0098\",\n            \"P0120\",\n            \"P0239\",\n            \"P0260\",\n            \"P0333\",\n            \"P0428\",\n            \"P0465\"\n          ],\n          \"limitations\": \"解耦证据主要来自回顾性分析，尚未通过干预试验证实；'毒性预示疗效'的现象可能受混杂因素（如肿瘤负荷、体能状态）影响。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"微生物干预策略的安全性及供体特征的情境依赖性\",\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"重点分析 FMT-LUMINate 试验数据：FMT 联合 ICI 在 NSCLC（ORR 80%）和黑色素瘤（ORR 75%）中显示高疗效，但黑色素瘤双药组严重 irAEs 达 65%（P0197, P0583）。\",\n            \"揭示供体特异性毒性风险：Prevotella 富集供体（Cluster B）在双 ICI（抗 PD-1+CTLA-4）背景下与心肌炎风险增加相关（15% 发生率），但在单药抗 PD-1 背景下未观察到类似毒性（P0197, P0583, Tool Material）。\",\n            \"讨论益生菌的双向作用：特定共生菌（如 Akkermansia）增强疗效，而外源性益生菌（如 LGG）可能缓解毒性但存在免疫抑制患者风险（P0040, P0357）。\",\n            \"评估抗生素与 PPI 的干扰：抗生素暴露不仅降低疗效，也增加严重结肠炎风险（P0310, P0417）；PPI 联用可能增加肝胆及皮肤毒性报告率（P0088）。\"\n          ],\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0040\",\n            \"P0088\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0310\",\n            \"P0357\",\n            \"P0417\",\n            \"P0583\"\n          ],\n          \"limitations\": \"FMT 毒性信号主要来自小样本 II 期试验，机制未完全解析（如 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎的具体分子通路）；益生菌菌株特异性强，商业制剂风险需警惕。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"微生物介导毒性的潜在分子机制\",\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"屏障功能与易位：菌群失调（如 Akkermansia 减少）导致 LPS 易位激活 TLR4/NF-κB 通路，加剧肠道损伤（P0217, P0361）。\",\n            \"代谢物介导：甲萘醌（维生素 K2）生物合成增强可能通过抑制 NF-κB 发挥保护作用（P0308）；SCFAs 通过表观遗传修饰调节 Treg/Th17 平衡（P0124, P0472）。\",\n            \"免疫细胞激活：微生物通过 MyD88 通路激活巨噬细胞产生 TNFα/IL-6 导致肝损伤，或激活 CD8+ T 细胞导致 IFNγ炎症（P0126）；ICI 诱导心肌炎依赖 CD8 T 细胞来源的 TNF 信号（P0149）。\",\n            \"分子模拟：细菌抗原与宿主自身抗原交叉反应可能触发自身免疫反应（P0267, P0462）。\"\n          ],\n          \"source_handles\": [\n            \"P0124\",\n            \"P0126\",\n            \"P0149\",\n            \"P0217\",\n            \"P0267\",\n            \"P0308\",\n            \"P0361\",\n            \"P0462\",\n            \"P0472\"\n          ],\n          \"limitations\": \"机制证据多来自动物模型或体外实验，人体内直接验证有限；代谢物在肿瘤微环境中的浓度数据缺失，多为血浆代理。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"supplement_requests\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定 T 细胞亚群）在 FMT-LUMINate 研究中仅表现为相关性，是否有后续研究解析其下游信号通路？\",\n          \"reason\": \"当前材料仅确认了关联及治疗背景的情境依赖性，缺乏机制解析，需确认是否有新进展以支撑机制章节的论述。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"是否有针对非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究，以验证 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的样本量小或证据不足的问题？\",\n          \"reason\": \"当前证据高度集中于结肠炎，其他毒性类型的微生物预测标志物证据薄弱，需确认是否存在被遗漏的关键研究。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n          \"reason\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0017\",\n          \"reason\": \"该研究提供了 FMT 小鼠模型验证结肠炎因果关联的强证据，需明确其实验设置与人类临床数据的对应关系。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0025\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦于 ADC 联合 ICI 的毒性，无微生物组数据，仅能提供背景毒性基线，与本章微生物调节主题不符。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0099\",\n      \"reason\": \"主要讨论内分泌毒性临床管理，微生物组证据仅为概念性提及，无实证数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0299\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦血液病及牙周 - 肠轴，与实体瘤 ICI 治疗场景差异较大，机制外推风险高。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0318\",\n      \"reason\": \"建立 OST 毒性评分系统，无微生物组数据，仅能作为临床表型背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0373\",\n      \"reason\": \"讨论分子成像技术，微生物组成像处于探索阶段，无实质性关联数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0405\",\n      \"reason\": \"比较 HCC 与其他实体瘤的肝毒性，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0465\",\n      \"reason\": \"建立毒性分级系统预测预后，无微生物组数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0539\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦血液系统恶性肿瘤，虽机制有类比价值，但临床数据不直接适用于实体瘤综述。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 6 of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nThe specific chapter is \"Ch6: 微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\" (Association between Microbiome and Immunotherapy Toxicity).\nI need to produce a JSON output containing the chapter proposal, including title, purpose, scope, substantive threads, source handles, etc., based on the provided source routing and shared outline.\n\nKey constraints:\n1.  **Language**: Chinese.\n2.  **Format**: JSON only.\n3.  **Content**: Focus on substantive knowledge and analysis, not just intro/summary.\n4.  **Scope**: Solid tumors, ICI (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4), gut microbiome, irAEs (toxicity).\n5.  **Evidence**: Distinguish observational vs. causal, human vs. animal, specific tumor types.\n6.  **Sources**: Use the provided `source_routing` ledger. Do not discard routed sources unless genuinely out of scope (list in `excluded_source_handles`).\n7.  **Structure**: Follow the `shared_level1_outline` for Ch6 but refine based on evidence.\n8.  **Specific Focus**: irAEs prediction, efficacy-toxicity coupling/decoupling, donor characteristics (e.g., Prevotella) and context dependence (ICI regimen).\n9.  **Limitations**: Acknowledge gaps (e.g., mechanism of Prevotella cardiotoxicity, lack of Phase III RCTs for toxicity management).\n10. **No \"Intro/Summary\" chapters**: This is Ch6, so it should be substantive.\n11. **Source Handles**: Use the provided handles (e.g., P0011, P0017, P0197, etc.).\n12. **Tool Material**: Incorporate the FMT-LUMINate data from `chapter_tool_materials`.\n\nPlan for Ch6:\n1.  **Title**: 微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联 (Association between Microbiome and Immunotherapy Toxicity).\n2.  **Purpose**: Analyze the link between gut microbiome features and irAEs, discuss the efficacy-toxicity trade-off, and evaluate predictive biomarkers and intervention safety.\n3.  **Substantive Threads**:\n    *   **Microbiome Signatures for irAEs**: Specific taxa associated with colitis, myocarditis, etc. (e.g., Ruminococcaceae, Bacteroides, Prevotella). Distinguish tumor types (GI cancer vs. Melanoma/NSCLC).\n    *   **Efficacy-Toxicity Coupling**: Does better response mean more toxicity? Role of microbiome in this balance (e.g., Akkermansia).\n    *   **Intervention Safety (FMT/Probiotics)**: Risks associated with microbiome modulation (e.g., FMT-LUMINate cardiotoxicity with Prevotella-rich donors in dual ICI).\n    *   **Mechanisms**: Barrier function, metabolites (SCFAs, Tryptophan), immune cell modulation (Tregs, Th17).\n    *   **Context Dependence**: ICI regimen (mono vs. combo), tumor type, baseline microbiome.\n4.  **Sources**: Select relevant ones from the routing list (P0011, P0017, P0029, P0049, P0082, P0197, P0239, P0308, P0583, etc.).\n5.  **Exclusions**: Sources purely about hematological malignancies without solid tumor relevance (e.g., P0299, P0539 might be limited but can be used for mechanism analogy if noted). P0025 (ADC+ICI) is relevant for background toxicity but not microbiome specific, keep for context.\n6.  **Tool Data**: Integrate FMT-LUMINate ORR and toxicity data (Prevotella/Cluster B).\n\nRefining the Outline based on Evidence:\n*   The shared outline asks for \"prediction\", \"coupling/decoupling\", \"donor characteristics\".\n*   Evidence notes highlight FMT-LUMINate (Prevotella + dual ICI = myocarditis risk).\n*   Need to emphasize that microbiome-toxicity links are often observational and context-dependent.\n*   Distinguish between colitis (most studied) and other irAEs (myocarditis, endocrine, etc.).\n\nDrafting the JSON:\n*   `chapter_id`: \"Ch6\"\n*   `title`: \"微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\"\n*   `purpose`: ...\n*   `scope`: ...\n*   `substantive_threads`: List of themes with specific source handles and analysis points.\n*   `excluded_source_handles`: List sources that are truly out of scope (e.g., purely hematological without mechanism overlap, or purely ADC toxicity without microbiome).\n*   `supplement_requests`: If any critical data is missing (e.g., specific metabolite concentrations in TME for toxicity).\n*   `directed_reads`: If any specific papers need deep dive (though routing is done).\n\nLet's check the source routing for Ch6 specific assignments:\nP0011, P0017, P0025, P0029, P0040, P0049, P0051, P0062, P0072, P0082, P0088, P0098, P0099, P0119, P0120, P0124, P0126, P0136, P0144, P0148, P0149, P0164, P0165, P0171, P0182, P0192, P0197, P0202, P0212, P0214, P0217, P0225, P0231, P0239, P0248, P0253, P0255, P0259, P0260, P0261, P0267, P0273, P0278, P0284, P0298, P0299, P0304, P0308, P0310, P0312, P0313, P0314, P0316, P0318, P0322, P0325, P0333, P0338, P0341, P0353, P0357, P0358, P0359, P0361, P0373, P0383, P0385, P0405, P0417, P0423, P0428, P0433, P0434, P0462, P0464, P0465, P0472, P0504, P0505, P0530, P0539, P0543, P0554, P0563, P0564, P0567, P0568, P0583, P0585.\n\nMany sources are assigned to Ch6. I need to select the most relevant ones for the substantive threads to avoid overcrowding, but the instruction says \"Preserve the broad set of useful source handles assigned by routing; do not collapse chapters to a few deep-read seed papers.\" So I should list the relevant handles in the threads or as available material. I will group them by theme in `substantive_threads`.\n\nI need to make sure I don't just list sources but explain *what* they contribute to the argument.\nI need to incorporate the FMT-LUMINate tool data explicitly.\nI need to ensure limitations are stated within the threads (e.g., observational nature, tumor specificity).\n\nStructure of `substantive_threads`:\n1.  **Microbiome Signatures Predicting irAEs**: Focus on colitis (P0017, P0072, P0278) and other irAEs (P0051, P0099). Mention inconsistency (P0049, P0312).\n2.  **Efficacy-Toxicity Coupling**: The \"double-edged sword\" (P0082, P0239, P0260, P0428). Akkermansia example (P0260).\n3.  **Intervention Safety & Donor Context**: FMT risks (P0197, P0583 - Tool Data), Probiotics (P0040, P0357). Prevotella/Cardiotoxicity context (Dual ICI vs Mono).\n4.  **Mechanistic Pathways**: Barrier, Metabolites, Immune cells (P0120, P0124, P0149, P0308).\n5.  **External Modulators**: Antibiotics, PPIs affecting toxicity (P0310, P0088, P0417).\n\nI will exclude sources that are purely about hematological malignancies with no solid tumor mechanism overlap (e.g., P0299, P0539 might be excluded or used with heavy caveat). P0025 is about ADC+ICI toxicity, useful for background but not microbiome specific, I'll keep it for context setting but note limitation. P0099 is about endocrine irAEs with little microbiome data, might be excluded or used for clinical context. Let's keep most but note limitations.\n\nActually, the instruction says \"When an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\". P0025 (ADC+ICI) is not about microbiome, so it might be out of scope for a *microbiome* review chapter unless used strictly for baseline toxicity comparison. I will exclude it to keep focus on microbiome. P0099 (Endocrine irAEs) has little microbiome data, exclude. P0299 (Periodontal/Hematological) is too far, exclude. P0539 (Hematological) exclude. P0316 (TCM) is relevant for intervention but maybe too specific, keep if discussing interventions. P0325 (TCM) similar. I will keep TCM sources if they discuss microbiome mechanism.\n\nLet's refine the excluded list to only those truly irrelevant to *gut microbiome* and *solid tumor ICI toxicity*.\nP0025 (ADC+ICI, no microbiome) -> Exclude.\nP0099 (Endocrine irAEs, minimal microbiome) -> Exclude.\nP0299 (Periodontal/Hematological) -> Exclude.\nP0539 (Hematological) -> Exclude.\nP0318 (OST score, no microbiome) -> Exclude.\nP0405 (Liver injury, no microbiome data) -> Exclude.\nP0465 (Toxicity grading, no microbiome) -> Exclude.\nP0530 (Neurological toxicity, explicitly says no specific microbiome signature) -> Can be used to state the gap, but maybe exclude if no positive finding. I'll keep it to state the gap.\nP0373 (Imaging, no microbiome data) -> Exclude.\n\nOkay, let's construct the JSON.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":30434,"completion_tokens":5388,"total_tokens":35822,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2630,"text_tokens":5388},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":30434}},"created":1791138092,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-96fcd8a9-b90a-908a-a40e-0dfd38d34776"}